note right of d4
  **One widget, many places (§4.6.3 rule 2).** The **same** `factory` value may
  appear in several instances that differ only in `surface_id`; there is never one
  version of a widget per screen.

  **When in doubt, start as a probe:** an unproven widget is a `DEV_PROBE` on the
  `developer` surface first, and becomes a panel of its mode when the user wants
  it there. That is what ADR D4 means in practice. The `dev_board` surface that
  first carried this rule, and mirrored the trading rail, was deleted with the Dev
  Board in `EPIC-033P`.
end note

note bottom of b2
  **Every screen is a surface (§4.6.3 rule 3).** Because `backtest` declares
  `accepts = {RAIL, MODAL}`, `strategy` and `market_data` can place instances on it
  **without `backtesting` importing either module**.
end note

note bottom of w1
  What is about the application itself belongs to the **shell**, not to a
  module: today the Developer page of Tools → Options. The `welcome` and
  `settings` surfaces were deleted by EPIC-033C and EPIC-033E.

  A guard renders the *UI map* — the set of these instances keyed by
  (surface_id, place) — and fails on a factory contributed nowhere, or on a
  `place` literal that does not exist.
end note
@enduml
